Package: kite-storage
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: KiteOS builder <root@localhost>
Depends: bash, apt, dpkg, coreutils, diffutils, util-linux, e2fsprogs, udev, yad, pkexec, sudo
Recommends: mate-polkit | lxpolkit, libnotify-bin
Description: KiteOS — keep apps and their data on an external disk
 "Apps & Storage" (kite-apps) and the kite-storage command install apps on
 the internal disk and then, if you choose, copy their program files and/or
 their settings and data to an external USB/SD disk and link them back with
 symlinks. Moved apps keep upgrading normally; APT refuses to touch them
 while the disk is unplugged, and their launchers explain what is missing.
